module

public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.AffineScheme
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Crystalline.SmallSite.RestrictionCalculus

/-!
# The restriction covers by affine opens are cofinal on the small crystalline site

Fix a global crystalline situation `(p, (S, I, γ), X)`.  The topology of the small crystalline
site `Cris(X/S)` is generated by the coverage of families of restrictions `A|_V ⟶ A` of an object
to an open cover of its ambient scheme,
`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.restrictCoverage_toGrothendieck`.  This file proves that
the families in which every member of the open cover is an **affine** open are already cofinal:
every covering sieve of every object `A` of `Cris(X/S)` is refined by a family of restrictions of
`A` to affine opens of its ambient scheme.

The statement needs no affineness hypothesis on `A` itself, because the affine opens of any scheme
form a basis.  What the proof gives is the sharper pointwise form: a covering sieve of `A`
contains the structure morphism `A|_V ⟶ A` of the restriction to *some* affine open neighbourhood
`V` of any prescribed point of the ambient scheme of `A`.

This is the cofinality hypothesis `hCovCofinal` of the Čech criterion
`Stacks.CechSite.subsingleton_ext_of_cechCohomology_isZero` ([Stacks, Tag 03F9] with the morphism
universe of the site free), whose system of coverings `Cov` is here `affineRestrictCoverings`.
The other hypothesis of that criterion which is about the coverings alone, the existence of the
iterated fibre products, is also supplied, from
`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite.CrystallineThickening`'s
`hasProduct_restrictOpenCover`.

## Main results

* `SmallSite.CrystallineThickening.exists_le_and_preimage_eq` — an open of the ambient scheme of
  `A|_V` is the preimage of an open of the ambient scheme of `A` below `V`, affine if it is.
* `SmallSite.CrystallineThickening.sieve_restrictOpenHom_of_restrictOpenHom_comp` — a sieve on `A`
  containing a restriction of a restriction contains the corresponding restriction of `A`.
* `SmallSite.CrystallineThickening.exists_isAffineOpen_mem_restrictOpenHom_mem_of_saturate` — the
  pointwise cofinality statement, by induction over `CategoryTheory.Coverage.Saturate`.
* `SmallSite.CrystallineThickening.exists_isAffineOpen_restrictOpenCover_le` — every covering
  sieve of `A` is refined by a family of restrictions of `A` to affine opens covering its ambient
  scheme.
* `SmallSite.affineRestrictCoverings` — those families, in the shape the Čech criterion indexes
  its system of coverings by, with `SmallSite.affineRestrictCover` building its members.
* `SmallSite.affineRestrictCoverings_cofinal` — **the cofinality hypothesis of
  `Stacks.CechSite.subsingleton_ext_of_cechCohomology_isZero`**, verbatim.
* `SmallSite.hasProduct_of_mem_affineRestrictCoverings` — the iterated-fibre-product hypothesis
  `hProducts` of the same criterion, verbatim.

## Implementation notes

`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.CrystallineThickening` is an `abbrev` for an
`CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.FullSubcategory`, so dot notation `A.foo` on an object of
`Cris(X/S)` resolves only against that namespace: `A.restrictOpen`, `A.restrictOpenHom` and
`A.restrictOpenCover` are available that way, while `restrictOpenLE`, `restrictOpenMap` and
everything in
`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite.CrystallineThickening` must be applied
prefix-style, `restrictOpenLE A h`.

The induction is over `CategoryTheory.Coverage.Saturate` for `restrictCoverage`, which is the
shape of the private `coverage_refine_saturate` in
`StacksFrontier/CategoryTheory/Sites/Cohomology/FibredCategory/FibreHomologySheafification.lean`.
That argument is reproduced rather than reused, and no public general version is extracted,
because its two typeclass hypotheses both fail for `restrictCoverage`:
`CategoryTheory.Precoverage.HasIsos` would ask the singleton presieve of an isomorphism
`Y ⟶ A` to be a family of restrictions, and `Precoverage.IsStableUnderComposition` would ask a
restriction of a restriction to be literally a restriction.  Both hold only up to the canonical
isomorphism `SmallSite.CrystallineThickening.isoRestrictOpenRestrictOpen`, and a refinement
statement phrased with sieve membership — as the pointwise statement here is — absorbs those
isomorphisms, since a sieve is closed under precomposition.  The general version would in any
case only produce a refinement by *some* family of restrictions; the affineness is what is
wanted, and it comes from the affine opens of a scheme being a basis,
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isAffineOpen_mem_and_subset`.

The transitive step is where the restriction-of-a-restriction calculus is used.  The inner
induction hypothesis produces an affine open `W` of the ambient scheme of `A|_V`; the open of the
ambient scheme of `A` it corresponds to is its image under the open immersion of `V`, and
`exists_le_and_preimage_eq` is phrased as the existence of an open whose *preimage* is `W` so
that the correspondence can be substituted, avoiding any transport along an equality of opens.

Of the hypotheses of `Stacks.CechSite.subsingleton_ext_of_cechCohomology_isZero`, the one this
file does not address is `hCovObjects`: the ambient scheme of the fibre product of a finite
subfamily must again belong to the collection `B`.  By
`SmallSite.CrystallineThickening.leftIsoRestrictOpenIInf` that fibre product is the restriction
to an intersection of affine opens, so it is the affineness of such an intersection —
`AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineOpen.iInf`, which needs separatedness of the ambient scheme — that is
still required.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07IG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07IG)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03F9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03F9)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry TopologicalSpace
open scoped AlgebraicGeometry

universe u

noncomputable section

namespace Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite

namespace CrystallineThickening

variable {S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}}

/-! ### Opens of the ambient scheme of a restriction -/

/-- **The structure morphism of a restriction is an open immersion on ambient schemes.**  This is
`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.Thickening.isOpenImmersion_restrictOpenHom_targetHom`,
recorded for the morphism of `Cris(X/S)` so that `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.opensRange` and
the image of an open are available for it. -/
instance isOpenImmersion_restrictOpenHom_hom_targetHom (A : CrystallineThickening S)
    (V : A.obj.thickening.target.scheme.Opens) :
    IsOpenImmersion (A.restrictOpenHom V).hom.targetHom.hom :=
  inferInstanceAs (IsOpenImmersion (A.obj.restrictOpenHom V).targetHom.hom)

/-- **An open of the ambient scheme of `A|_V` is the preimage of an open of the ambient scheme of
`A` lying below `V`**, namely of its image under the open immersion of `V`, which is affine as
soon as it is.  The statement is phrased as the existence of a preimage rather than as the image
itself, so that a consumer may substitute the identification instead of transporting along it. -/
theorem exists_le_and_preimage_eq (A : CrystallineThickening S)
    {V : A.obj.thickening.target.scheme.Opens}
    (W : (A.restrictOpen V).obj.thickening.target.scheme.Opens) :
    ∃ V' : A.obj.thickening.target.scheme.Opens, V' ≤ V ∧
      (IsAffineOpen W → IsAffineOpen V') ∧
      (A.restrictOpenHom V).hom.targetHom.hom ⁻¹ᵁ V' = W := by
  refine ⟨(A.restrictOpenHom V).hom.targetHom.hom ''ᵁ W,
    (Scheme.Hom.image_le_opensRange _ W).trans
      (Thickening.restrictOpenHom_targetHom_opensRange A.obj V).le,
    fun hW ↦ hW.image_of_isOpenImmersion _, Scheme.Hom.preimage_image_eq _ W⟩

/-- **A sieve on `A` containing the composite of the structure morphisms of `(A|_V)|_{V'}` and of
`A|_V` contains the structure morphism of `A|_{V'}`.**  The two differ by the isomorphism
`isoRestrictOpenRestrictOpen`, and a sieve is closed under precomposition. -/
theorem sieve_restrictOpenHom_of_restrictOpenHom_comp (A : CrystallineThickening S)
    {V V' : A.obj.thickening.target.scheme.Opens} (h : V' ≤ V) {R : Sieve A}
    (hR : R ((A.restrictOpen V).restrictOpenHom
      ((A.restrictOpenHom V).hom.targetHom.hom ⁻¹ᵁ V') ≫ A.restrictOpenHom V)) :
    R (A.restrictOpenHom V') := by
  have key : (isoRestrictOpenRestrictOpen A h).hom ≫ A.restrictOpenHom V' =
      (A.restrictOpen V).restrictOpenHom
        ((A.restrictOpenHom V).hom.targetHom.hom ⁻¹ᵁ V') ≫ A.restrictOpenHom V := by
    rw [← restrictOpenLE_restrictOpenHom A h,
      isoRestrictOpenRestrictOpen_hom_restrictOpenLE_assoc]
  rw [← key] at hR
  have h2 := R.downward_closed hR (isoRestrictOpenRestrictOpen A h).inv
  rwa [← Category.assoc, Iso.inv_hom_id, Category.id_comp] at h2

/-! ### Cofinality of the restriction covers by affine opens -/

/-- **A covering sieve of an object `A` of `Cris(X/S)` contains the restriction of `A` to an
affine open neighbourhood of any prescribed point of its ambient scheme.**

This is the pointwise form of the cofinality of the restriction covers by affine opens, proved by
induction over the saturation generating the topology from `restrictCoverage`.  In the base case
the covering family is already a family of restrictions, and an affine open inside the member
containing the point is produced by the affine opens being a basis.  In the transitive step the
inner induction hypothesis is applied to the restriction produced by the outer one, and
`exists_le_and_preimage_eq` together with
`sieve_restrictOpenHom_of_restrictOpenHom_comp` turns the resulting restriction of a restriction
into a restriction of `A`. -/
theorem exists_isAffineOpen_mem_restrictOpenHom_mem_of_saturate
    {A : CrystallineThickening S} {R : Sieve A}
    (hR : Coverage.Saturate (restrictCoverage S) A R) :
    ∀ x : A.obj.thickening.target.scheme, ∃ V : A.obj.thickening.target.scheme.Opens,
      IsAffineOpen V ∧ x ∈ V ∧ R (A.restrictOpenHom V) := by
  induction hR with
  | of B P hP =>
    intro x
    obtain ⟨I, V, hVcov, rfl⟩ := hP
    obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := hVcov x
    obtain ⟨W, hWaff, hxW, hWle⟩ := exists_isAffineOpen_mem_and_subset hi
    exact ⟨W, hWaff, hxW, _, restrictOpenLE B hWle, B.restrictOpenHom (V i), ⟨i⟩,
      restrictOpenLE_restrictOpenHom B hWle⟩
  | top B =>
    intro x
    obtain ⟨W, hWaff, hxW, -⟩ :=
      exists_isAffineOpen_mem_and_subset (U := ⊤) (x := x) trivial
    exact ⟨W, hWaff, hxW, trivial⟩
  | transitive B R₁ R₂ _ _ ih₁ ih₂ =>
    intro x
    obtain ⟨V, hVaff, hxV, hVR⟩ := ih₁ x
    obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ : x ∈ (B.restrictOpenHom V).hom.targetHom.hom.opensRange := by
      simpa using hxV
    obtain ⟨W, hWaff, hyW, hWQ⟩ := ih₂ hVR y
    obtain ⟨V', hV'le, hV'aff, rfl⟩ := exists_le_and_preimage_eq B W
    refine ⟨V', hV'aff hWaff, ?_,
      sieve_restrictOpenHom_of_restrictOpenHom_comp B hV'le hWQ⟩
    rw [← hy]
    exact hyW

/-- **Every covering sieve of an object `A` of `Cris(X/S)` is refined by the family of
restrictions of `A` to a cover of its ambient scheme by affine opens.**  The refinement is
indexed by the points of the ambient scheme, lifted to the universe a covering family of the
crystalline site indexes over. -/
theorem exists_isAffineOpen_restrictOpenCover_le {A : CrystallineThickening S} {R : Sieve A}
    (hR : R ∈ smallTopology S A) :
    ∃ V : ULift.{u + 1} A.obj.thickening.target.scheme →
        A.obj.thickening.target.scheme.Opens,
      (∀ i, IsAffineOpen (V i)) ∧ (∀ x : A.obj.thickening.target.scheme, ∃ i, x ∈ V i) ∧
        (A.restrictOpenCover V).sieve₀ ≤ R := by
  classical
  rw [← restrictCoverage_toGrothendieck] at hR
  choose V hVaff hVmem hVR using
    exists_isAffineOpen_mem_restrictOpenHom_mem_of_saturate (Coverage.mem_toGrothendieck.mp hR)
  refine ⟨fun i ↦ V i.down, fun i ↦ hVaff i.down, fun x ↦ ⟨ULift.up x, hVmem x⟩, ?_⟩
  intro Z k hk
  obtain ⟨Y, g, f, ⟨i⟩, rfl⟩ := hk
  exact R.downward_closed (hVR i.down) g

end CrystallineThickening

/-! ### The cofinal system in the shape the Čech criterion consumes -/

/-- The family of restrictions of an object `A` of `Cris(X/S)` to a family of affine opens
covering its ambient scheme, as an element of the subtype of covering families of `A` that
`Stacks.CechSite.subsingleton_ext_of_cechCohomology_isZero` indexes its system `Cov` by. -/
def affineRestrictCover {S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}} (A : CrystallineThickening S)
    {I : Type (u + 1)} (V : I → A.obj.thickening.target.scheme.Opens)
    (hcov : ∀ x : A.obj.thickening.target.scheme, ∃ i, x ∈ V i) :
    { E : PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} A // E.sieve₀ ∈ smallTopology S A } :=
  ⟨A.restrictOpenCover V, smallZariskiCovering_mem_smallTopology S (A.restrictOpenCover V)
    (A.isZariskiCovering_restrictOpenCover V hcov)⟩

/-- The underlying covering family of `affineRestrictCover A V hcov` is `A.restrictOpenCover V`. -/
@[simp]
theorem affineRestrictCover_coe {S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}}
    (A : CrystallineThickening S) {I : Type (u + 1)}
    (V : I → A.obj.thickening.target.scheme.Opens)
    (hcov : ∀ x : A.obj.thickening.target.scheme, ∃ i, x ∈ V i) :
    (affineRestrictCover A V hcov).1 = A.restrictOpenCover V :=
  rfl

/-- **The system of coverings of the small crystalline site by restrictions to affine opens**, in
the shape `Stacks.CechSite.subsingleton_ext_of_cechCohomology_isZero` takes its system `Cov`:
for each object `A` of `Cris(X/S)`, the covering families of `A` presented by the restrictions of
`A` to a family of affine opens covering its ambient scheme. -/
def affineRestrictCoverings {S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}} (A : CrystallineThickening S) :
    Set { E : PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} A // E.sieve₀ ∈ smallTopology S A } :=
  {E | ∃ (I : Type (u + 1)) (V : I → A.obj.thickening.target.scheme.Opens),
    (∀ i, IsAffineOpen (V i)) ∧ (∀ x : A.obj.thickening.target.scheme, ∃ i, x ∈ V i) ∧
      E.1 = A.restrictOpenCover V}

/-- **A family of restrictions of `A` to affine opens covering its ambient scheme belongs to the
system `affineRestrictCoverings`.** -/
theorem affineRestrictCover_mem_affineRestrictCoverings
    {S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}} (A : CrystallineThickening S) {I : Type (u + 1)}
    (V : I → A.obj.thickening.target.scheme.Opens) (hV : ∀ i, IsAffineOpen (V i))
    (hcov : ∀ x : A.obj.thickening.target.scheme, ∃ i, x ∈ V i) :
    affineRestrictCover A V hcov ∈ affineRestrictCoverings A :=
  ⟨I, V, hV, hcov, rfl⟩

/-- **The restriction covers by affine opens are cofinal in the topology of `Cris(X/S)`**: every
covering sieve of every object is refined by one of them.  This is the hypothesis `hCovCofinal`
of `Stacks.CechSite.subsingleton_ext_of_cechCohomology_isZero` for the system
`affineRestrictCoverings`, stated verbatim; the collection `B` of objects plays no role, the
affine opens of a scheme being a basis whether or not that scheme is affine. -/
theorem affineRestrictCoverings_cofinal (S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u})
    (B : Set (CrystallineThickening S)) :
    ∀ A ∈ B, ∀ R ∈ smallTopology S A,
      ∃ E : { E : PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} A // E.sieve₀ ∈ smallTopology S A },
        E ∈ affineRestrictCoverings A ∧ E.1.sieve₀ ≤ R := by
  intro A _ R hR
  obtain ⟨V, hVaff, hVcov, hVle⟩ :=
    CrystallineThickening.exists_isAffineOpen_restrictOpenCover_le hR
  exact ⟨affineRestrictCover A V hVcov,
    affineRestrictCover_mem_affineRestrictCoverings A V hVaff hVcov, hVle⟩

/-- **The iterated fibre products of a covering by restrictions to affine opens exist**, in the
slice category `Over A`.  This is the hypothesis `hProducts` of
`Stacks.CechSite.subsingleton_ext_of_cechCohomology_isZero` for the system
`affineRestrictCoverings`, stated verbatim; it is
`SmallSite.CrystallineThickening.hasProduct_restrictOpenCover`. -/
theorem hasProduct_of_mem_affineRestrictCoverings {S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}}
    {A : CrystallineThickening S}
    (E : { E : PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} A // E.sieve₀ ∈ smallTopology S A })
    (hE : E ∈ affineRestrictCoverings A) (p : ℕ) (i : Fin (p + 1) → E.1.I₀) :
    HasProduct fun a ↦ Over.mk (E.1.f (i a)) := by
  obtain ⟨E, hEcov⟩ := E
  obtain ⟨I, V, -, -, rfl⟩ := hE
  exact CrystallineThickening.hasProduct_restrictOpenCover A V p i

end Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite

end

end
